# Matthee2023_EIGER_z6p1
# Paper: Matthee et al. 2023, ApJ 950, 67 (EIGER II), doi:10.3847/1538-4357/acc846; arXiv:2211.08255 (v3 checked)
# Source: Table 1, column log(Phi_corr) (completeness- and Vmax-corrected field LF; the log(Phi_obs) column is not used)
# Redshift: 5.33 < z < 6.96 ("z~6" in the paper); z = 6.30-6.35 around the quasar J0100+2802 is masked.
#   File labelled z = 6.1 (bin midpoint 6.15, volume-weighted mean 6.12).
# Line: [O III] lambda5008; bins of 0.2 dex (centres listed); single NIRCam/WFSS field (25.9 arcmin^2)
# Cosmology: H0 = 67.4, Om = 0.315 (Planck18)
# Note: only sources with completeness > 10% are used (84 objects). Errors combine Poisson noise with a
#   25% completeness/volume uncertainty in quadrature.
#
# Columns:
# Log10(L_[OIII]5008 / erg s^-1)
# Log10(Phi / cMpc^-3 dex^-1)
# Lower 1-sigma delta in dex
# Upper 1-sigma delta in dex
